course: dictionary
lesson: 11303
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word yawning can mean two different things, and the words around it tell you which one. Read the context first, then test your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
explain: «Yawning, heavy eyes and clumsiness are signs of tiredness.» Here yawning is something your mouth does: you open it wide and take a deep breath, often without meaning to, because you are tired. The clue is tiredness.
explain: «...a 2 am game, however great the craic, means a yawning, foggy day at school.» Here yawning describes the day. It is a describing word, an adjective, and it tells you the day will feel sleepy and dull.
explain: Yawning can also mean very wide and open, like a yawning gap or a yawning cave. Look for the word that is describing a gap, cave or hole.
fact: Yawning means opening your mouth wide and taking a deep breath, usually when you are tired or bored.
fact: Yawning is a reflex, so your body does it on its own.
fact: Yawns are catching: when someone near you yawns, you may yawn too.
fact: As an adjective, yawning means very wide and open, like «a yawning gap» or «a yawning cave».
fact: Always yawning in class can mean you need more sleep. Cover your mouth when you yawn to be polite.
exercise: «Yawning, heavy eyes and clumsiness are signs of tiredness.» What is yawning in this sentence? | Shouting loudly in class | A huge gap in the ground | Running very fast | *Opening your mouth wide and breathing deeply, because you are tired
exercise: In which phrase does yawning mean very wide and open? | Stop yawning, please | Cover your mouth | Yawning and stretching in bed | *A yawning gap
exercise: Why should you cover your mouth when you yawn? | *To be polite to the people around you | To stop your teeth from growing | To make your yawn louder | So you can yawn for longer
test: In «a 2 am game ... means a yawning, foggy day at school», what is the day like? | Full of music | Bright and busy | *Sleepy and dull | Cold and snowy
test: Yawns are catching. What does that mean? | Yawning makes you run faster | Yawns can be caught like a cold | You must catch a yawn in your hand | *When one person yawns, others often yawn too
exam: Which sentence uses yawning as a describing word? | *A yawning gap opened in the wall | She stopped yawning and smiled | Yawning, heavy eyes are signs of tiredness | I am yawning in class
